{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/294692-the-most-epic-game-youre-or-you-have-run-so-far","id":294692,"title":"The most epic game youre or you have run so far.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-28T04:42:26-07:00","id":294692,"title":"The most epic game youre or you have run so far.","content":"I was talking to one of my players and we stablished one of her characters (a Imbued redeemer who is a couple of a nuwisha) and the campaing i ran was pretty emotionally devastating but was excelent. thing is i got inspired (while running V20) and i offered my player to come back with that trademark character (not as a hunter, as a human) and making her couple a human as well. she accepted...thing is...im pretty much gonna run <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Crow </div> </div> </div> i mean <i><u>Risen</u></i> and the idea is getting me very thrilled so far...<br /> <br /> what are your experiences ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T06:23:52-07:00","id":294751,"title":"","content":"Officialy, kinfolk can't become Imbued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T07:10:14-07:00","id":294792,"title":"","content":"Man, I've run and participated in a few monstrously epic cWoD games. I guess I'll have to say my now-defunct Vampire game which went from 16 BC to 800 AD, in which the characters were 5th generation in Genoa, was the most epic. That chronicle got to see the rise of Western Christianity, the end of the Roman Empire, several invasions on Northern Italy, and featured Ashur, Japheth, Montano and several other Methuselahs as regular characters, among other insane things. Good times!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1506-lubricus","name":"Lubricus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T08:26:43-07:00","id":294863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/294692-the-most-epic-game-youre-or-you-have-run-so-far?p=294751#post294751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Officialy, kinfolk can't become Imbued.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> She was an imbued, she meet a werecoyote. she was a redeemer and she saw that he was more human that most humans and slowly started to get attached to him so...well.... five tequila shots later and a wedding on mexico..<br /> <br /> besides..GOLDEN RULE!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 10-28-2014, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T12:27:27-07:00","id":295068,"title":"","content":"Uktena Kinfolk, learned to become a Sorcerer, made a deal with a demon for more power to help his sept when they were in trouble, died while fighting a corrupted mokole during a skirmish with the local pentex subsidiary. Demon took over his body 'saving him', reeked havok covertly for months but was destoryed in a battle with the sept he used to be part of; but not before they bound the soul of the demon and his own into a gem. Black Spiral Dancers later raided the sept in a different stroyline and during the raid they stole the gem. Near the end of like 2 or 3 arcs later the big bad finally showed his face with a wicked bane klaive with none other then that gem mounted to the hilt. During the fight the klaive was destroyed and the gem broke open releasing the now fully combined soul of what was the demon and my characters soul but fueled with pure wyrm energy. The spirit merge with a dead garou on the battlefield, this new creature went on to become the new big bad for the next chronicle.<br /> <br /> It was our unintentional version of Samual Haight, he just kept becoming the perfect source of turmoil for the different storylines my troupe came up with,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T17:43:11-07:00","id":295447,"title":"","content":"For me, it was just one event in Werewolf that'll always stick out. Great big battle at a strip mine, following a tangent after the Rite of Passage module; several packs from two septs involved. The characters, newly cliaths, were supposed to guard the rear and had a couple claymores (the explosives) that the Glass Walker procured.<br /> <br /> ...They took down a big bad by throwing one into the blades of her helicopter while she was escaping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T21:57:52-07:00","id":295626,"title":"","content":"I played a Kuei-Jin. He started out as a Devil-Tiger. He ended up causing someone to become a Shih. He ended up enslaving a wraith. Raising a bastet. Siring a dhampir. Creating a circle of fomoris. An earthbound and he warred with one another and he had a frenemy with a mage. His life was epic in all of it's glory and ended up being an akuma. From there, he would drive out the Sabbat from some small towns in Nevada and consolidating it as a network of dragon-nests. He also had to force the garou to GTFO. His goal was to ring in the new age himself and try to reclaim his soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-31T09:21:24-07:00","id":298223,"title":"","content":"Played a True Brujah that was being hunted by a clan of Vampires made by Angels to hunt his Sire and clan to extinction. Group was a bunch of 5th gens that soloed their army of ancillae and neonates and I killed the Antediluvian and his Elders. Elders died in one turn and the Antediluvian the next, I then diablerized him and became the True Brujah Antediluvian. Went around time traveling and basically became the Doctor. Got Arcane and shit, was a legend amongst legends. Never went into Torpor and was good buddies with Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}